**A model answer.** The changed function in `tests/registration-helpers.ts`:

```ts
export async function fillRegistrationForm(page: Page, email: string, phone: string = '5551234567') {
  await page.goto('https://demo.automationtesting.in/Register.html');

  await page.getByPlaceholder('First Name').fill('Ada');
  await page.getByPlaceholder('Last Name').fill('Lovelace');
  await page.locator('textarea').fill('12 Engine Street');
  await page.locator("input[type='email']").fill(email);
  await page.locator("input[type='tel']").fill(phone);

  await page.getByLabel('FeMale').check();
  await page.locator('#checkbox1').check();

  await page.locator('#Skills').selectOption('Java');
  await page.locator('#country').selectOption('India');
}
```

`tests/practice-phone.spec.ts`:

```ts
import { test, expect } from '@playwright/test';
import { fillRegistrationForm } from './registration-helpers';

test('the form is filled with a phone number of its own', async ({ page }) => {
  await fillRegistrationForm(page, 'katy@example.com', '5559876543');
  await expect(page.locator("input[type='tel']")).toHaveValue('5559876543');
});
```

Run both spec files with `npx playwright test tests/register-helper.spec.ts tests/practice-phone.spec.ts --project=chromium`:

```output
Running 3 tests using 3 workers

[1/3] [chromium] › tests\register-helper.spec.ts:9:5 › the form is filled for Grace
[2/3] [chromium] › tests\register-helper.spec.ts:4:5 › the form is filled for Ada
[3/3] [chromium] › tests\practice-phone.spec.ts:4:5 › the form is filled with a phone number of its own
  3 passed (4.5s)
```

**What to check in your own answer.** The two tests in `register-helper.spec.ts` still call the helper with an email only, and they still pass, because the default value fills the Phone field when a call leaves the phone out. The alternative, a second function named for the phone, would hold a second copy of the ten lines, and the two copies would drift apart at the first change to the form. Your times, and the order of the three lines, may be different.
